## 2. Operational Mandates
1. **Native Progressive Disclosure & `/context` Verification (`< 50 Lines` Root)**: Keep `AGENTS.md` strictly `< 50 lines` with standard links (never `@[...]` inline expansion in `AGENTS.md`, which causes the Token Bloat Trap). All `.agents/rules/*.md` files must reside at the top level of `.agents/rules/` (or be registered in `.agents/rules.json` to avoid the Silent Discard Trap) and carry valid snake_case YAML frontmatter (`trigger: model_decision` + `description`, avoiding the Broken Frontmatter Trap). Run `/context` to inspect active rules and token usage; convert repetitive procedures into Skills (`.agents/skills/`).
2. **Mandatory Memory Bootstrapping & Infrastructure Compliance**: On `/start`, ingest `memory-bank/*.md` and adhere to [Infrastructure Invariants](memory-bank/infrastructureInvariants.md), [Cluster Invariants](.agents/rules/infra.md), and [Negative Constraints](.agents/rules/negative-constraints.md).
3. **On-the-Fly Context Registration, Pre-Authenticated Access & Continuous Cycling (`< 150 Lines`)**:
   - **Pre-Authenticated MCP & Customizations Access (Zero Redundant Prompts)**: All MCP servers, host token files (`~/.github_token`, `~/.stripe_token`, `~/.stitch_token`, `~/.ovh_credentials.json`, `~/.meta_credentials.json`, `~/.meta_token`), CLI/OAuth sessions (`~/.azure/`, `~/.linkedin_mcp/`, `~/Library/Application Support/mj/`, `~/.mcp-auth/`), and `.env*` keys marked `✅ AUTHENTICATED` in [Integrations & Customizations](memory-bank/integrationsAndCustomizations.md) are pre-authorized (`AGENT_PERMISSION_PRESET_TURBO`). **NEVER redundantly ask the user for API keys, tokens, logins, or permission—invoke `call_mcp_tool` or read indexed credentials directly.**
   - **Zero-Manual-Step Registration & Lifecycle Hooks**: Immediately distill pertinent architectural decisions, keys, MCPs, or domain rules into `memory-bank/*.md` (`< 150 lines` each). `.agents/hooks.json` (`SessionStart`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`) and `.git/hooks/post-commit` auto-run `node scripts/sync-memory-context.mjs --quiet`. Upon `/update-memory`, run Phase 1 (Closure & Sync) then Phase 2 (Auto-Start banner).
4. **Passive Observer Invariant**: `memory-bank/*.md` is strictly a read-only passive observer. Active tickets, sprint boards, and bug records live in `docs/backlog.json` and `docs/BACKLOG.md`.
5. **Decoupled Backlog & Context-Frugal Execution**: Capture tasks/attachments offline (`npm run backlog add/attach/actions` or Review pane `backlog.html`). Execute via `[/backlog-start](.agents/skills/backlog-start/SKILL.md)` (`FEAT-101`), which unpacks attachments, runs tests, and syncs `docs/backlog.json` + `memory-bank/` without sacrificing code quality, UX fidelity, or verification rigor.
6. **Strict End-to-End Verification Before Closure**: NEVER mark any ticket involving third-party integrations, OAuth providers, or external credentials as `done` until live server credentials are configured and a real end-to-end integration test passes; otherwise keep `in_progress`.
7. **Lock Down `/plan` Before Coding (`Explore → Plan → Execute`) & 3-Artifact Correlation**: Never jump straight into editing files for complex features or multi-file bugs—run `/plan` or `[/backlog-plan](.agents/skills/backlog-plan/SKILL.md)` first to lock down and review `implementation_plan.md` (**Goal Description**, **User Review Required**, **Proposed Changes**, **Verification Plan**), `task.md`, and `walkthrough.md` in `<brainDir>/` and `docs/planning/` correlated 1-to-1 with `docs/backlog.json`.
8. **Stop the Credit Bleed & Strict Token Frugality (`≤ 8 Tool Turns per Fix`)**:
   - **Prune Aggressively with `/clear`, `/compact` & `/context`**: Run `/clear` (then `/start`) or `/compact` immediately after finishing every sub-task or bug fix so 50k-token build histories never carry into the next task (~95% per-turn cost reduction). Use `/context` to inspect active rules and loaded files.
   - **Throttle Reasoning with `/effort` & Disable Overage Toggle**: Use `/effort` (`low`/`medium`) for boilerplate UI, routing, or simple CRUD, and reserve `high` `/effort` for complex state/architecture logic. Keep the Google One / Antigravity **"Toggle for overage"** disabled (hard stop at 20x baseline limit) and check `/credits` & `/usage` to monitor model drain.
   - **Memory-First Lookup**: Check [Active Context](memory-bank/activeContext.md) and [Local Backlog JSON](docs/backlog.json) before running diagnostics; never re-investigate recorded state.
   - **Never Read `transcript.jsonl` or Sibling Repos**: Strictly forbid reading `.system_generated/logs/transcript*.jsonl` or grepping sibling repos (`BinaryDay`, `SnapCal`, `RemoveBackGround`, `AntigravityRemote`) unless explicitly requested.
   - **Hard Turn Budget (`≤ 8 Tool Turns per Fix`)**: Batch all file reads into 1 turn, all edits into 1–2 turns, and all verification/deployment commands into 1–2 chained shell calls.

